+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop. It has four pages (home, books, events and visit), a genre-filterable catalog, and a contact form that validates input but does not send anything.
+
+Plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. No build step, no dependencies, no external requests: no CDNs, web fonts or remote images. Fonts are system font stacks.
+
+## Structure
+
+- `index.html`, `books.html`, `events.html`, `visit.html` at the repo root
+- `css/styles.css` shared styles
+- `js/nav.js` mobile menu, `js/books.js` genre filter (state in `?genre=`), `js/visit.js` form validation
+- `tests/run.mjs` headless Chrome tests
+
+## Run the site
+
+From the repo root:
+
+```sh
+python3 -m http.server 8000
+```
+
+Then open http://localhost:8000/ in a browser. JavaScript is required.
+
+## Run the tests
+
+The tests use Playwright and Chrome at `/usr/bin/google-chrome`. Playwright must be resolvable from Node, for example installed globally. Nothing is added to the repo.
+
+```sh
+node tests/run.mjs          # every check
+node tests/run.mjs books    # one group: nav, books, events, visit or site
+```
+
+The runner starts its own static server on a free port, checks every page for console errors, off-origin requests, a 360px width with no sideways scrolling, nav behaviour, the catalog filter and URL state, and the form, and exits non-zero on failure.
+
+## Notes
+
+- The contact form validates name, email and message in the browser. On success it says that no message was sent; it makes no network request.
+- Genre values in the URL must match a genre name exactly. Anything else, including a different case, shows the full catalog.
